{%- comment -%}
  AJ Past Deals — what you missed.

  Two jobs on a store whose whole proposition is "come back tomorrow".

  PROOF. A first-time visitor has no way to know whether the daily deal is a
  real daily rhythm or a banner that has sat there for a month. A visible run
  of previous deals, each with a date, answers that without claiming anything.

  RETURN VISITS. Showing a genuinely good deal that has closed is the honest
  version of urgency — nothing is being withheld or faked, the offer simply
  happened and the next one will too.

  DEMAND. Each card can register interest in a return. Deliberately a SIGNAL and
  not a sale: letting someone buy an expired Yoink at its old price would make
  the countdown on today's deal a lie — nothing would ever really be gone, and a
  repeat visitor learns that fast. That spends the one mechanism the store runs
  on. Asking "do people want this back?" gets the same information and keeps the
  promise.

  The MISSED numbers lead — the discount stamped across the image, the old deal
  price, and the saving spelled out — because a card that does not land as a loss
  gives nobody a reason to ask for it back or to check earlier tomorrow.

  What keeps that honest rather than bait-and-switch is labelling: ENDED across
  the whole image, the deal price struck through and captioned GONE, and today's
  real price stated plainly beside it. A large unqualified "$24" on something that
  now costs $40 would read as the current price, and discovering otherwise at
  checkout is the kind of surprise that loses a customer permanently. Urgency from
  a true fact, never an ambiguous one.

  Sorting is done by hand because Liquid's `sort` cannot reach a metaobject
  field, so entries are packed into "epoch^index" strings, sorted as text
  (fixed-width epochs sort correctly), and reversed for newest-first.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script src="{{ 'aj-bring-back.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>

{%- liquid
  assign now = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign limit = section.settings.max_deals | plus: 0
  comment
    Within the last week a weekday reads the way someone actually thinks about it
    ("Saturday's Yoink"); older than that a weekday is ambiguous, so use a date.
  endcomment
  assign week_ago = now | minus: 604800
-%}

{%- capture packed -%}
  {%- for entry in shop.metaobjects.daily_deal.values -%}
    {%- assign ends = entry.ends_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0 -%}
    {%- if ends <= now and entry.product.value != blank -%}
      {{ ends }}^{{ forloop.index0 }}~
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign packed_list = packed | split: '~'
  assign sorted = packed_list | sort | reverse
  assign shown_count = 0
-%}

{%- if sorted.size > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="aj-past color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} section spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  >
    <div class="page-width">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="aj-past__heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-past__subheading">{{ section.settings.subheading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <ul class="aj-past__grid" role="list">
        {%- for key in sorted -%}
          {%- if shown_count >= limit -%}
            {%- break -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- assign wanted = key | split: '^' | last | plus: 0 -%}
          {%- assign ended_epoch = key | split: '^' | first | plus: 0 -%}

          {%- for entry in shop.metaobjects.daily_deal.values -%}
            {%- unless forloop.index0 == wanted -%}
              {%- continue -%}
            {%- endunless -%}

            {%- liquid
              assign past_product = entry.product.value
              assign past_price = entry.deal_price.value
              assign current_variant = past_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
              assign votes = entry.bring_back_votes.value | plus: 0
              assign shown_count = shown_count | plus: 1

              if ended_epoch >= week_ago
                assign day_label = entry.ends_at.value | date: '%A'
                assign day_suffix = "'s Yoink"
              else
                assign day_label = entry.ends_at.value | date: '%b %-d'
                assign day_suffix = ''
              endif

              comment
                The discount it ran at, measured against the supplier MSRP where
                there is one — a genuine list price and the bigger number — and
                against our own price otherwise. Stamped on the image because the
                percentage is the part that stings.
              endcomment
              assign past_deal_cents = entry.deal_price.value | times: 100
              assign past_anchor = current_variant.compare_at_price
              if past_anchor == blank or past_anchor <= current_variant.price
                assign past_anchor = current_variant.price
              endif
              assign past_off = 0
              if entry.deal_price.value != blank and past_anchor > past_deal_cents
                comment
                  Round explicitly. deal_price is a decimal metafield, so
                  `times: 100` yields a float and Liquid's divided_by then keeps
                  full precision — it rendered "37.30569948186528% off" on the
                  live site.
                endcomment
                assign past_off = past_anchor | minus: past_deal_cents | times: 100.0 | divided_by: past_anchor | round
              endif
            -%}

            <li class="aj-past__item">
              <p class="aj-past__day">{{ day_label }}{{ day_suffix }}</p>
              <a class="aj-past__link" href="{{ past_product.url }}">
                <span class="aj-past__media">
                  {%- if past_product.featured_media -%}
                    {{
                      past_product.featured_media
                      | image_url: width: 500
                      | image_tag:
                        loading: 'lazy',
                        sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 25vw, 45vw',
                        widths: '200, 300, 400, 500',
                        class: 'aj-past__image',
                        alt: past_product.featured_media.alt
                    }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Across the whole image, not a corner badge. A small stamp
                    competes with the product for attention; the card needs to
                    read "over" before anything else is processed, so the missed
                    deal lands as a miss. Fades on hover so the product is still
                    inspectable — someone deciding whether to ask for it back
                    needs to see what it is.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <span class="aj-past__veil" aria-hidden="true">
                    {%- if past_off > 0 -%}
                      <span class="aj-past__wasoff">{{ past_off }}% off</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    <span class="aj-past__stamp">Ended</span>
                  </span>
                </span>
                <span class="aj-past__title">{{ past_product.title | escape }}</span>
              </a>

              {%- comment -%}
                The missed deal price LEADS. The job of this section is to make a
                shopper feel they missed something worth having — that is what
                makes them ask for it back and check earlier tomorrow. Leading
                with today's price buries the only number that does that.

                It is struck through, captioned GONE, and today's real price sits
                beside it. A large unqualified "$24" on something that now costs
                $40 reads as the current price, and finding out otherwise at
                checkout is the kind of surprise that loses a customer for good.
                The urgency comes from a true fact, not an ambiguous one.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign deal_cents = past_price | times: 100
                assign missed_cents = current_variant.price | minus: deal_cents
              -%}

              <p class="aj-past__meta">
                {%- if past_price != blank and missed_cents > 0 -%}
                  <span class="aj-past__gone">
                    <s class="aj-past__dealprice">{{ deal_cents | money }}</s>
                    <span class="aj-past__gonelabel">discounted price</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="aj-past__now">
                    {{ current_variant.price | money }}
                    <span class="aj-past__nowlabel">regular price</span>
                  </span>
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="aj-past__now">{{ current_variant.price | money }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>

              {%- if past_price != blank and missed_cents > 0 -%}
                <p class="aj-past__missed">You missed {{ missed_cents | money }} off</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- assign past_ship = past_product.metafields.ship.cost.value -%}
              {%- if past_ship != blank and past_ship == 0 -%}
                <p class="aj-card-free">Ships free</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if section.settings.show_bring_back -%}
                <aj-bring-back class="aj-past__bringback" data-deal-id="gid://shopify/Metaobject/{{ entry.system.id }}">
                  <button type="button" class="aj-past__vote">
                    {{ section.settings.bring_back_label | default: 'Bring back this deal' }}
                  </button>
                  <span
                    class="aj-past__votes"
                    data-vote-count
                    {% if votes == 0 %}hidden{% endif %}
                  >
                    {%- if votes == 1 -%}
                      1 person wants this back
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ votes }} people want this back
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                </aj-bring-back>
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
  <div class="aj-past aj-past--empty page-width">
    <p>
      <strong>No deals have finished yet.</strong>
      Past deals appear here automatically once their end time passes.
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{{ 'aj-ships-free.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{% stylesheet %}
  .aj-past__heading {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }

  .aj-past__subheading {
    margin: 0 0 var(--padding-md, 1.5rem);
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .aj-past__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--padding-md, 1.5rem);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-past__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(12rem, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .aj-past__item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .aj-past__link {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .aj-past__media {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--aj-tile-radius, 8px);
    background: var(--aj-tile-well, rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.04));
  }

  .aj-past__image {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    /* Was `cover`, which cropped — the only surface still doing so once the
       grid cards were fixed. The dimming below is what makes these read as
       past; the crop was never carrying that meaning, it was just the value
       this file happened to be written with. */
    object-fit: var(--aj-tile-fit, contain);
    display: block;
    /* History, not merchandise — but this section's job is to make a card land
       as a LOSS, and that needs the product to still look worth having. There
       is no regret without desire.

       It was dimmed three times over: full desaturation, 38% transparency, AND
       the 42% ink veil above. Any one of those reads as past; all three read as
       dead, which is the opposite of the intended feeling.

       The veil stays, because it is what guarantees the white "81% off" is
       legible over an arbitrary product photo. The other two go: half
       desaturation is enough to keep today's live deal unmistakably the thing
       to act on, while leaving the product recognisable as something you wanted.

       Half also matters on mobile, where the hover restore below never fires —
       the resting state is the only state most people will see. */
    filter: grayscale(0.45);
    transition: filter 0.2s ease, opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .aj-past__link:hover .aj-past__image,
  .aj-past__link:focus-visible .aj-past__image {
    /* opacity is no longer set at rest, so there is nothing to restore. */
    filter: grayscale(0);
  }

  .aj-past__day {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .aj-past__bringback {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-block-start: 0.2rem;
  }

  .aj-past__vote {
    padding: 0.35em 0.75em;
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.4);
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: none;
    color: inherit;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .aj-past__vote:hover:not([disabled]),
  .aj-past__vote:focus-visible {
    border-color: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb));
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.07);
  }

  .aj-past__vote[disabled] {
    opacity: 0.55;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .aj-past__votes {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .aj-past__veil {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.42);
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  /* Larger than the ENDED stamp: the discount is what registers as a loss, the
     stamp only explains why it is unavailable. */
  .aj-past__wasoff {
    color: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb));
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .aj-past__stamp {
    padding: 0.3em 0.9em;
    border: 2px solid rgb(var(--color-background-rgb));
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb));
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    /* Rotated so it reads as a stamp over the picture rather than as a caption
       belonging to it. */
    transform: rotate(-6deg);
  }

  .aj-past__link:hover .aj-past__veil,
  .aj-past__link:focus-visible .aj-past__veil {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .aj-past__title {
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: var(--aj-tile-clamp, 2);
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  /*
    THESE ARE SCREEN-READER LABELS AND WERE PRINTING ON THE PAGE.

    `.aj-past__gonelabel` and `.aj-past__nowlabel` carry "discounted price" and
    "regular price" so a screen reader can tell two bare numbers apart. They had
    no CSS at all, so they rendered as visible text and every card read
    "$136.98 discounted price $249.05 regular price" — which is not a sentence
    anyone would write, and buried the one figure the section exists to land.

    Clipped rather than `display: none`, because none removes them from the
    accessibility tree too and the labels would stop doing their actual job.
  */
  .aj-past__gonelabel,
  .aj-past__nowlabel {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  .aj-past__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  /*
    "now" IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT DECORATION.

    The line renders two bare numbers: a struck $136.98 and a bold $249.05. On
    every other storefront a struck price is the HIGHER one, so this reads as a
    price rise — the struck figure here is the deal that ended, and the bold one
    is what it costs today.

    The markup already carried "discounted price" / "regular price" to say so,
    but those were screen-reader labels printing on the page, and clipping them
    took the meaning with them. Three characters put it back for sighted users
    without the clumsiness, and the clipped labels still do the work for anyone
    listening.
  */
  .aj-past__now::before {
    content: 'now ';
    font-weight: 400;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .aj-past__now {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /*
    The card bottom was ragged: uneven gaps between title, prices, the missed
    line and the button, made worse by only some cards carrying a "Ships free"
    badge or a vote count. One consistent rhythm, and the vote count reserved
    space whether or not it has any, so a row of cards does not step up and down.
  */
  .aj-past__missed {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  /*
    AFTER the blanket child rule above, deliberately. That rule sets a margin on
    every child including this one, and at equal specificity the later rule
    wins — which silently undid the `auto` that pushes the button to the bottom
    of the card and put every button back at a different height.
  */
  .aj-past__bringback {
    margin-block-start: auto;
    padding-block-start: 0.75rem;
  }

  .aj-past__votes {
    display: block;
    min-height: 1.1rem;
  }

  /*
    KEEP THE SLOT, DROP THE WORDS.

    The vote count carries `hidden` when nothing has been voted for, and setting
    `display: block` above overrode the browser's [hidden] rule — so every card
    started announcing "0 people want this back", which is both noise and a
    quietly discouraging thing to say about a product.

    visibility rather than display: the line stops rendering but its space is
    still reserved, so a row of cards does not step up and down depending on
    which deals happen to have votes. That reservation is the whole reason the
    min-height above exists.
  */
  .aj-past__votes[hidden] {
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .aj-past__was {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .aj-past__date {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .aj-past--empty {
    padding-block: var(--padding-xl, 3rem);
    text-align: center;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Past Deals",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows recently finished deals, newest first. Hidden until at least one deal has ended."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Recent deals"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Subheading",
      "default": "A new one every day. Here's what you missed."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_deals",
      "label": "Deals shown",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Bring it back"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_bring_back",
      "label": "Let shoppers ask for a Yoink back",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Registers interest only. Selling an expired Yoink at its old price would make today's countdown meaningless."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "bring_back_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "Bring back this deal"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 32
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "AJ Past Deals"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
